{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Let my father arise and eat of his son's game.</b> Jacob spoke in the language of entreaty — 'קוּם נָא שְׁבָה' — for נָא is nothing but a request, and furthermore he told him to sit and to eat; he spoke with him in direct address. But Esav did not tell him to arise from the place where he was standing and to sit in the place prepared for eating, nor did he mention the word נָא, but spoke in an obscure manner because of the exceeding haughtiness of his heart."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:26.140511406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}